# Content-versioned assets, cached for a year (2026-07-29).
#
# Every reference to these carries ?v=<ASSET_VERSION>, so the URL itself changes
# whenever the file does and the browser fetches the new one immediately. They
# were on a four-hour revalidate, which meant a returning visitor re-checked
# roughly seven versioned files per page for no benefit - the URL had already
# told them nothing changed.
#
# The one risk is an edit that ships without a version bump: that would pin the
# stale file for a year. scripts/verify-asset-version.js fingerprints each of
# these and fails the ship if the bytes moved and ASSET_VERSION did not, so the
# bump cannot be forgotten. Keep that script's IMMUTABLE list in step with this
# block.
#
# data.js is deliberately excluded - it is the venue dataset, it changes on
# nearly every ship, and a gate that fires every time is a gate nobody reads.
/styles.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/venue.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/site-ui.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

